{"name":"Tan","hex":"#d1b26f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tan","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A Chinese surname from Mandarin."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A Chinese surname from Hokkien."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trigonometric functions","blocks":[{"text":"In mathematics, the trigonometric functions are real functions which relate an angle of a right-angled triangle to ratios of two side lengths. They are widely used in all sciences that are related to geometry, such as navigation, solid mechanics, celestial mechanics, geodesy, and many others. They are among the simplest periodic functions, and are widely used for studying periodic phenomena through Fourier analysis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Academ_Base_of_trigonometry.svg/330px-Academ_Base_of_trigonometry.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trigonometric_functions"},{"title":"Kult (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Kult is a Polish rock band formed in 1982 in Warsaw."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Kult_-_concert_in_Warsaw.jpg/330px-Kult_-_concert_in_Warsaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kult_(band)"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Taylor_cos.gif/500px-Taylor_cos.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimed